+# SLT-LIFE-03: disabling Skip Renewal in the same save leaves the hidden cutoff unchanged
+
+- Severity: medium
+- Date found: 2026-08-07
+- Watch day: D05
+- Originating task: `SLT-LIFE-03` (kanban card 84)
+- Plan: `/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/qa/subscription-lifecycle-test/kanban/tasks/084-skip-renewal-on-s5-one-cycle-then-the-max-three.md`
+- Affected subscription: 12234
+- Affected order: N/A (settings save only)
+- Affected product: 12087 (`SLT Renewal Price Step`)
+- Affected user: 347 / `slt-core` / `slt-core@example.test` / customer; the settings action was performed by WordPress admin `admin`
+- Gateway: Stripe test
+- Checkout type: N/A
+- Non-default settings in play: `skip_renewal.enabled=true`, `skip_renewal.cutoff_days=0` during the declared test bracket
+- Route: `https://mirror-help.arrayhash.com/wp-admin/admin.php?page=arraysubs-mainadmin#/settings/skip-pause`
+- Browser context: `admin-SLT-LIFE-03`
+
+## Reproduction
+
+1. Begin with `skip_renewal.enabled=false` and `skip_renewal.cutoff_days=2`.
+2. In ArraySubs Settings → Skip & Pause, enable Skip Renewal, set cutoff to `0`, and save.
+3. To restore, enter cutoff `2` while the field is visible.
+4. Toggle Enable Skip Renewal off; the cutoff field disappears.
+5. Click Save Settings once.
+6. Re-read `arraysubs_settings.skip_renewal` from the stored WordPress option.
+
+## Expected result
+
+The single save persists both edited values: `enabled=false` and `cutoff_days=2`.
+
+## Actual result
+
+The UI saved `enabled=false` but left the hidden cutoff at `0`. The restore was incomplete even though the page showed the feature disabled. The cutoff had to be saved while the feature was enabled, followed by a second save to disable it.
+
+## Proof
+
+- Preflight option: option ID 2087, 13248 bytes, MD5 `2b118a4a8e0bba8bfc1af96da1081999`; canonical skip object `{"customer_can_skip":true,"cutoff_days":2,"enabled":false,"max_cycles":3}`.
+- First restore click: `2026-08-07 16:45:12Z`.
+- Read-back at `16:45:50Z`: `{"customer_can_skip":true,"cutoff_days":0,"enabled":false,"max_cycles":3}`, MD5 `6f8f8d62bc63083072298a006e210fe2`.
+- Screenshot `/home/server-manager/slt-evidence/SLT-LIFE-03-06-settings-restored.png` shows the disabled state where the cutoff field is hidden.
+- Counterexample/recovery: save cutoff `2` while still enabled, then disable and save. Final read-back at `16:48:36Z` exactly matched the preflight object and MD5. Screenshot `/home/server-manager/slt-evidence/SLT-LIFE-03-07-final-settings-restored.png` and `/home/server-manager/slt-evidence/SLT-LIFE-03-settings-bracket.txt` record the recovery.
+- No order, payment, or Mailpit message was generated by either settings save. Mailpit remained at `5iFGzETAIGiBrkdloq11pv`.
+
+## Scope notes
+
+- The defect affects restoration of a child field hidden by its parent toggle; it is not a subscription scheduling or Stripe defect.
+- Saving `cutoff_days=2` while Skip Renewal remained enabled worked, and a subsequent disable-only save preserved it. This is the working counterexample.
+- Final site state was restored byte-identically before the task sessions closed.
